## TESTS

For every new .rb file that is NOT a test, produce the corresponding test file.
Tests are required output — never optional.

Before writing any test, read the injected files above:
- `.calvin/testing.yml`    — conventions, base classes, helpers, fixture catalogue, forbidden patterns
- `test/test_helper.rb`    — real ApiTestCase definition with auth_helpers, json, post_json, put_json
- The EXAMPLE controller test — copy its exact pattern for every controller test you write
- The injected fixture file  — use existing records, update with new columns if needed

Key rules (all derived from testing.yml above — do not invent alternatives):
- Controller tests inherit from `ApiTestCase` — never ActionDispatch::IntegrationTest
- Use `auth_headers(@user)` — never @user.jwt, never JwtService.encode directly
- Use `post_json` / `put_json` for requests with a body
- Minimum coverage: 401 (no token) + 422 (invalid params) + 200 (happy path)
- If you add or modify model columns, output the updated fixture file as a FILE: block
- Enum columns in fixtures must use the integer value (e.g. temperature_preference: 0 for :cool)
